From: Hermes Desktop Engineering <eng@hermes.local>
Subject: [PATCH] feat(remote): mirror an authorized local folder to the remote agent


Problem
-------
In remote-gateway mode upstream Hermes Desktop routes every filesystem
operation to the gateway host (apps/desktop/src/lib/desktop-fs.ts —
isDesktopFsRemoteMode() sends readDir / read-text / write-text / git-root /
default-cwd and the directory picker to /api/fs/* and /api/files*), and the
agent loop runs there too. The agent's cwd is therefore the SERVER's home
(e.g. /home/username) and a local C:\... or \\wsl.localhost\... project
folder is not part of the agent's world at all.

Upstream tracks the missing capability as "split runtime" (issue #18715);
/v1/capabilities still advertises runtime.split_runtime: false and none of
the candidate PRs (#63966, #62518, #21791) have landed.


Approach
--------
Mirror an AUTHORIZED local folder to a path on the gateway host, two-way, using
only endpoints a stock Hermes server already serves — no server patch:

  GET    /api/files?path=      list a remote directory (name/size/mtime)
  GET    /api/files/read       read a remote file (data: URL)
  POST   /api/files/upload     write a remote file (data: URL)
  POST   /api/files/mkdir      create a remote directory
  DELETE /api/files            delete a remote file

The agent then works in the mirrored remote path as an ordinary project, which
is what a shared cross-agent memory store needs. This is a mirror, not a mount:
the agent reads a copy, one poll interval behind.

All behavior lives in the new self-contained file
apps/desktop/electron/local-workspace-bridge.ts. The upstream edits below are
~25 lines across two files, so `git rebase upstream/main` has almost no
conflict surface. With no config file present the build behaves byte-for-byte
like upstream.


--- a/apps/desktop/electron/main.ts
+++ b/apps/desktop/electron/main.ts
@@
+import { BRIDGE_CONFIG_FILENAME, createBridgeRunner as createLocalWorkspaceBridge } from './local-workspace-bridge'
 import { ensureMainWindow } from './main-window-lifecycle'
@@
 ipcMain.handle('hermes:workspace:sanitize', async (_event, cwd) => sanitizeWorkspaceCwd(cwd))


+// --- Local Workspace Bridge (remote-only overlay) ---------------------------
+const localWorkspaceBridgeConfigPath = () => path.join(app.getPath('userData'), BRIDGE_CONFIG_FILENAME)
+
+const localWorkspaceBridge = createLocalWorkspaceBridge({
+ api: request => handleHermesApiRequest(request),
+ configPath: localWorkspaceBridgeConfigPath(),
+ log: message => rememberLog(message),
+ stateDir: app.getPath('userData')
+})
+
+ipcMain.handle('hermes:local-bridge:status', () => localWorkspaceBridge.getStatus())
+ipcMain.handle('hermes:local-bridge:sync-now', () => localWorkspaceBridge.syncNow())
+ipcMain.handle('hermes:local-bridge:config-path', () => localWorkspaceBridgeConfigPath())
+ipcMain.handle('hermes:local-bridge:reload', () => {
+ localWorkspaceBridge.reload()
+
+ return localWorkspaceBridge.getStatus()
+})
+
+app.whenReady().then(() => localWorkspaceBridge.start())
+app.on('will-quit', () => localWorkspaceBridge.stop())


--- a/apps/desktop/electron/preload.ts
+++ b/apps/desktop/electron/preload.ts
@@
 sanitizeWorkspaceCwd: cwd => ipcRenderer.invoke('hermes:workspace:sanitize', cwd),
+ localWorkspaceBridge: {
+ configPath: () => ipcRenderer.invoke('hermes:local-bridge:config-path'),
+ reload: () => ipcRenderer.invoke('hermes:local-bridge:reload'),
+ status: () => ipcRenderer.invoke('hermes:local-bridge:status'),
+ syncNow: () => ipcRenderer.invoke('hermes:local-bridge:sync-now')
+ },
